    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "World Book Day falls on April 23 every year. What books are you going to read to celebrate this day? I would like to suggest that you read novels, because there are many benefits to reading them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Reading novels can provide fun and relaxation. It is good for both your physical and mental health. People who read novels have lower stress levels than those who don’t read. And novel readers have lower rates of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mental",
            "ref": "v-mental"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " illness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Different novelists have different "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "dialects",
            "ref": "v-dialect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and ways of speaking. When you read their works, you can learn new words and expressions. This can help you build your language skills."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Reading novels helps you to become more "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "empathetic",
            "ref": "v-empathetic"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". As you read, you learn about what happens to the characters and how it makes them feel. At the same time, certain areas of your brain become more active. You will feel as if you are experiencing the story yourself. According to one study, novel readers have higher levels of empathy than "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "nonfiction",
            "ref": "v-nonfiction"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " readers."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
